You can successfully get an elven dagger named Mjollnir, but that does
not make it an artifact.  Is a ninja-to what NetHack calls a broadsword
when you're a Samurai?  If so, *then* it is an artifact.

There are three ways to be sure you have an artifact:

1) If it's Stormbringer, or Sting, you can get special messages when
   weilding it.  (Attack messages with Stormbringer, Orc warnings with
   Sting.)

2) If you try to #name any artifact, it will resist the attempt.

3) Sell or buy it from a shop.  The price will reflect the value.  Artifacts
   are very worthy.

